    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>FloatyHeader lets you make any header or navbar sticky with ease. Target any class or ID and control how and when the header becomes sticky.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the ‘Plugins’ menu in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Go to &#8220;Settings &gt; FloatyHeader&#8221; and configure your options.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='can%20i%20target%20any%20header%3F'>\nCan I target any header?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, just enter the CSS class or ID of the element you want to make sticky.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='does%20this%20work%20with%20all%20themes%3F'>\nDoes this work with all themes?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, it works with all standard themes.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Make your WordPress headers sticky and customizable without code. Choose target element from the dashboard.",
